WEBVTT

00:00:28.939 --> 00:00:30.098
that helps us do work.

00:00:30.122 --> 00:00:32.530
So, of course, with lots
of programmable computers

00:00:32.554 --> 00:00:33.705
and robots around,

00:00:33.729 --> 00:00:35.561
this is an easy thing to picture.

00:00:35.585 --> 00:00:37.650
How many of you know
what I'm talking about?

00:00:37.674 --> 00:00:38.825
Raise your right hand.

00:00:38.849 --> 00:00:40.852
How many don't know
what I'm talking about?

00:00:40.876 --> 00:00:42.027
Raise your left hand.

00:00:42.051 --> 00:00:44.930
So that's great. So that was too easy.

00:00:44.954 --> 00:00:48.073
You guys have very insecure computers, OK?

00:00:48.097 --> 00:00:51.725
So now the thing is,
this is a different kind of spell.

00:00:51.749 --> 00:00:54.106
This is a computer program
made of zeros and ones.

00:00:54.130 --> 00:00:56.988
It can be pronounced on a computer,
does something like this.

00:00:57.012 --> 00:01:00.022
The important thing is we can write it
in a high-level language.